Qualifications
Minimum Qualifications
-Bachelor's degree or above, majoring in Computer Science, or related fields, with at least 1 year of experience building scalable systems;
-Experience in programming, included but not limited to, the following programming languages: C, C++, Java or Golang, C++ is a plus;
-Solid programming ability, excellent design and code style, enthusiastic about technical challenges;
-Effective communication skills and a sense of ownership and drive;
-Experienced in at least one area of the following areas: search engine, personalized recommendations, machine learning, distributed storage system, big data frameworks is a plus.

Job Summary
We are looking for a motivated and technically inclined individual to join a leading bank. This is an entry-level opportunity suitable for candidates with a foundation in Python programming and an interest in process automation. The successful candidate will support the development and implementation of automation solutions to streamline operational processes, reduce manual effort and improve data accuracy and efficiency.
Mandatory Skill-set
• Diploma or Degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, Data Analytics or a related discipline (candidates with relevant internship or project experience are welcome to apply);
• Must have basic to good knowledge of Python programming, with the ability to write and troubleshoot scripts;
• Familiarity with data handling and processing using Excel, CSV or other structured data formats;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with good attention to detail;
• Willingness to learn and work on practical automation solutions.
Desired Skill-set
• Exposure to Python libraries such as pandas, openpyxl or xlwings;
• Familiarity with Microsoft Excel, VBA, macros or Power Query;
• Basic knowledge of SQL and database operations;
• Exposure to process automation, data extraction, transformation or report generation;
• Familiarity with Microsoft Office applications, SharePoint or OneDrive;
• Previous internship or project experience involving Python development or automation would be an advantage.
Responsibilities
• Develop and implement Python-based automation solutions to streamline repetitive manual processes;
• Support the automation of data extraction, processing, transformation, validation, reconciliation and report generation;
• Work with business users and team members to understand existing workflows and identify opportunities for process improvement;
• Develop, enhance and troubleshoot automation scripts to improve processing efficiency and reliability;
• Perform testing and validation to ensure automated outputs are accurate and meet business requirements;
• Implement appropriate error handling, validation checks and processing logs to support operational controls;
• Investigate automation issues and assist with resolving technical problems;
• Prepare technical documentation and support knowledge transfer to ensure solutions can be maintained by the team.
